1. Bluetooth Module (e.g., HC-05)
VCC → 5V (Arduino)
GND → GND
TX → RX (Arduino)
RX → TX (Arduino) (use voltage divider if needed)
2. Relay Module (4-Channel)
VCC → 5V (Arduino)
GND → GND
IN1 → Arduino pin 2
IN2 → Arduino pin 3
IN3 → Arduino pin 4
IN4 → Arduino pin 5
3. Motors via Relay
Each motor uses 2 relays for direction control:
Motor A:
Relay 1 (IN1) → one terminal
Relay 2 (IN2) → other terminal
Motor B:
Relay 3 (IN3) → one terminal
Relay 4 (IN4) → other terminal
External battery (+) → relay COM terminals
Relay NO terminals → motor connections
Battery (−) → motor common return
4. Power
Arduino → separate 5V supply (or regulated)
Motors → external battery (do NOT power motors from Arduino)
